      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C201", "C198", "C183", "C161", "C160", "C170", "C195", "C193"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the exact query molecule.",
    "No query-specific efflux or intestinal-metabolism data; L5 records are for structurally related quaternary ammonium tropanes and other compounds.",
    "Query formulation, dose, prandial state, and salt form are unspecified.",
    "L3 trospium/glycopyrronium exposure records lack an IV comparator in these cards, so low Cmax/AUC alone does not fully separate absorption from clearance/distribution.",
    "The molecule_property_tool_summary reports neutral fraction 1 despite a quaternary ammonium nitrogen; this inconsistency limits reliance on the physicochemical prior."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low. Direct low-F evidence for quaternary ammonium/strong-cation small molecules and low oral exposure for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics support F < 20%. L5 adds mechanistic gut-wall evidence (uptake transporters, efflux, ion-pair effects) but no direct F result for the query; it does not provide affirmative evidence for F >= 20% and does not overturn the low prediction."
}

